    "title": "From the Mountains to Lake Norman: Wild Foraging Across North Carolina - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Robin Shupe Keller ,\n1 days ago There is a moment familiar to anyone who has truly learned to look at the woods — the moment the landscape stops being background and becomes a pantry. A shaded hollow reveals ramps. A mossy log fruits with oyster mushrooms. Wild onions push through the soil beside a trail. Across North Carolina, from the Blue Ridge Mountains to the shores of Lake Norman, that moment can happen almost anywhere. Read full article",
